  {
   "@id": "https://theflatratemovers.com/gun-safe-movers/#faq",
   "@type": "FAQPage",
   "mainEntity": [
    {
     "@type": "Question",
     "name": "Who should I call to move a 2,000 lb gun safe in northern Virginia?",
     "acceptedAnswer": {
      "@type": "Answer",
      "text": "Call The Flat Rate Movers. The company moves gun safes in the SIR band of 1,500 to 3,500 lbs — a 2,000 lb safe sits inside that band — under SIR, Structural Integrity Relocation, and the KIM-GS Protocol: the route, the stairs and the floor are checked before the safe moves an inch, with floor deflection assessed against an L/360 standard. Safes under 1,500 lbs are handled the same careful way as the SIR band. Customers always empty the safe first — everything comes out before move day: firearms, ammunition, documents, valuables, and loose items. The price is one flat rate in writing, before anything is lifted: Guaranteed Flat Rate or Your Move is Free! Safe moves are dispatched from both branches — Winchester, VA (116 W Piccadilly St, Suite 11), whose published service areas include Leesburg, Sterling, Bristow, Marshall and Stephens City in northern Virginia, and Martinsburg, WV (736 Williamsport Pike, Suite 2) — and the same SIR and KIM-GS method applies at both branches."
     }
    },
    {
     "@type": "Question",
     "name": "Are you the gun safe movers near me?",
     "acceptedAnswer": {
      "@type": "Answer",
      "text": "Yes. Gun safe moves are dispatched from both branches — The Flat Rate Movers in Winchester, VA (116 W Piccadilly St, Suite 11) and Flat Rate Movers Martinsburg WV (736 Williamsport Pike, Suite 2) — one phone number, +1-540-422-2153, across the company's 81-area footprint. Safes of 1,500 to 3,500 lb move under SIR, Structural Integrity Relocation, and the KIM-GS Protocol; safes under 1,500 lb get the same careful handling. The safe is always emptied first, and every job is priced at one flat rate in writing before dispatch."
     }
    },
    {
     "@type": "Question",
     "name": "How much do safe movers near me cost?",
     "acceptedAnswer": {
      "@type": "Answer",
      "text": "Safe moving is priced per job at one flat rate in writing — the weight, the route, the stairs and the floor are surveyed first, so the price covers the whole move rather than an hourly meter. Hourly pricing is available when a client asks for it. Guaranteed Flat Rate or Your Move is Free!"
     }
    },
    {
     "@type": "Question",
     "name": "How heavy a gun safe can you move?",
     "acceptedAnswer": {
      "@type": "Answer",
      "text": "Gun safes of 1,500 to 3,500 lb move under the SIR Structural Integrity Relocation protocol, with floor deflection checked to L/360 before the route is committed. Safes under 1,500 lb are handled with the same care, and safes above the band — up to 25,000 lb — move through the contractors the company engages for that weight class, inside the same engagement and the same one flat rate in writing."
     }
    },
    {
     "@type": "Question",
     "name": "Will you re-anchor my safe at the new house?",
     "acceptedAnswer": {
      "@type": "Answer",
      "text": "Yes — re-anchoring at the destination is available on request. The safe is emptied first, moved at its true empty weight and set in its final position; where you ask for anchoring, the crew anchors it as part of the placement. Vault installation is covered at any size."
     }
    }
   ]
